<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Old Prussians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Prussians (Baltic people), Baltic Prussians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Old Prussians were a Baltic people who lived between the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neman">Neman</a> on the south-eastern coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-sea">Baltic Sea</a>. Pagan into the 13th century, they were conquered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> between the 1230s and the 1280s after fierce resistance, and German and Polish settlers moved into their lands. Their language died out around 1700, but their name passed to the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/old-prussians.jpg" alt="Old Prussians" width="320" height="353" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MapMaster · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baltic_Tribes_c_1200.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Ottokar defeated Béla IV of Hungary at the Battle of Kressenbrunn in 1260, securing Styria, and joined the crusades of the Teutonic Knights against the pagan <b>Prussians</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Kingdom of Bohemia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>After King Andrew II of Hungary expelled the knights from the Burzenland in Transylvania in 1225, Duke Konrad I of Masovia invited them to help him against the pagan <b>Prussians</b> who were raiding his lands.</blockquote><a href="/empire/state-of-the-teutonic-order">State of the Teutonic Order · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Encouraged by the defeat of the Livonian Order and Teutonic Knights at Durbe, the <b>Old Prussians</b> rose against the Teutonic Order, each clan choosing its own leader, such as Herkus Monte of the Natangians.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/september-20">20 September in history</a></li><li><blockquote>They lived in farming communities ruled by local nobles with fortified places, and shared the religion and language of the other <b>Prussians</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/bartians">Bartians</a></li><li><blockquote>Exposed to raids by the pagan <b>Prussians</b> and Lithuanians, Konrad I invited the Teutonic Order in 1226 and gave it the land of Chelmno, a decision with lasting consequences.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-masovia">Duchy of Masovia</a></li><li><blockquote>Henry went on crusade to the Holy Land in 1154 and was killed fighting the pagan <b>Prussians</b> in 1166, after which the duchy passed to his brother Casimir II the Just.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-sandomierz">Duchy of Sandomierz</a></li></ul></section>
